  "description_text": "Perched on the coveted southwest slope of Queen Anne Hill this classic 1900 residence captures the essence of Pacific Northwest living where timeless warmth meets sunlit modernity and ever-changing views of Puget Sound, the Olympics, Alki and Bainbridge Island. Set behind a private, fenced front patio and gardens, tall ceilings, bespoke detailing, and glowing hardwoods welcome you into spaces made for connection. Afternoon light floods the expansive living room, drawing you toward walls of windows and a wide view deck built for sunset cocktails as ferries glide past. Host effortless dinners in the central dining room, linger with a book by the hearth in the fireside library, enjoy a movie in the main level den or retreat to the quiet main-floor office. Start mornings with coffee in the bright breakfast nook off the updated kitchen, featuring a gas range and stainless hood. A 3/4 bath is privately tucked nearby. Upstairs, wake to panoramic water vistas in the serene primary bedroom, joined by two generous secondary bedrooms, a dual-vanity bath and laundry. The high-ceiling daylight lower level adapts seamlessly to every chapter of life, from a sprawling rec room opening to a covered patio, to an en-suite guest bedroom, gym/flex space, storage, and a view bonus room plumbed for a second kitchen, ideal for multigenerational living or an ADU. Complete with a rare street-to-street lot, ample 9th Ave W parking, and easy access to transit and Queen Anne's vibrant shops and dining.",
